  "details": "Version: Dates several versions ago and still exists in this update.\n\nDescription of the bug: When switching avatars or firing an animation that exceeds the trigger collider or switching avatars (if the trigger is really small) causes the OnExitTrigger and OnEnterTrigger (if there is one next to it) events to fire even though your camera view is still physically still inside the trigger collider or the other trigger collider.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Go inside the trigger collider and not leave it (to properly test it\n2. Pull out an animation that exceeds the trigger colliders or collides with another one near it using an animation, gesture, or switching avatars.\n3. You can see in output logs that it fires the events even though you haven't physically left the collider you are in at all.",
